---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About PoolSavr: Who We Are and How the Math Works"
  description="Who is behind PoolSavr, how our pool volume calculations work, and what we're building next."
>
  <section class="border-b border-navy-100 bg-white py-12">
    <div class="container-page">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-5">
        <ol class="flex gap-2 text-sm text-navy-400">
          <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
          <li class="text-navy-700">About</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl sm:text-4xl">About PoolSavr</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
        PoolSavr publishes free pool calculators and is building a tool that
        measures pools from satellite imagery. This page explains how the math
        works and what state the product is actually in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white py-14">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl">Where we are right now</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            The volume calculator works today and is free. Enter your pool's
            dimensions and it returns gallons, surface area, and perimeter.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            The satellite measurement tool is not live yet. When it is, you will
            be able to skip the tape measure and get the same numbers from your
            address alone. We are not going to pretend it exists before it does.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl">How the calculations work</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            There is no proprietary trick here, and we would rather show the
            arithmetic than ask you to trust a black box. Volume is surface area
            multiplied by average depth, converted to gallons at 7.48052 gallons
            per cubic foot.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-900">Rectangular pools</strong> use exact
              geometry: length × width.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-900">Round and oval pools</strong> use the
              circle and ellipse area formulas.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-900">Kidney and freeform pools</strong> use
              an 0.85 factor against the bounding rectangle — the standard
              industry approximation, accurate to roughly 5%.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-900">Perimeter</strong> for oval shapes
              uses Ramanujan's ellipse approximation, which is accurate to well
              under 1% at pool proportions.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            Steps, benches, and tanning ledges are not subtracted. For chemical
            dosing that difference is negligible. For a paid drain-and-refill on a
            pool with a large ledge, it is worth accounting for by hand.
          </p>
          <a href="/calculators/pool-volume" class="btn-outline mt-6">
            Open the pool volume calculator
          </a>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl">What we will and won't do with your data</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            The calculator runs entirely in your browser. Nothing you type into
            it is sent anywhere — there is no account, no tracking of your
            dimensions, and no server involved.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            If you join the waitlist we keep your email and, if you give it, your
            ZIP code. The ZIP tells us which regions to cover first. We do not
            sell either one. See the
            <a href="/privacy" class="text-blue-600 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700">
              privacy policy
            </a> for the full detail.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl">Getting in touch</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            If a number looks wrong, or your pool shape is not covered, tell us —
            corrections to the calculator are the most useful mail we get. Reach
            us on the
            <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700">
              contact page
            </a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-blue-600 py-14">
    <div class="container-page text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl text-white">Want the satellite version?</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-blue-100">
        Leave your email and we'll tell you when address measurement goes live.
      </p>
      <Cta placement="header" variant="onBlue" class="mt-7" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
